<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimpapers yr shr surges, div increased.</title>
<headline>Zimpapers yr shr surges, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(all figures in Z$ million unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			 334.0     vs    122.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			 110.0     vs    25.0</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		48.37     vs    18.66</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   80.29     vs    31.24</p>
<p>    Tax				 31.92     vs    12.58</p>
<p>    Interest received		9.35     vs    0.79 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover			 401.28     vs    323.42</p>
<p>Div payable April 16</p>
<p>on register April 1</p>
<p>Full name: Zimbabwe Newspapers Group</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said although the planned launch of new newspapers and the importation of new printing equipment by its competitors presented challenges, its prospects remained firm on the back of a strong performance by the economy.</p>
<p>-- Harare newsroom +263-4 72 52 28/9</p>
